# Third-party skills installed by scripts/install-third-party.sh
# Format:  <github owner/repo>  <skill folder name>
# Lines starting with # are disabled. The script finds the folder by name and
# requires exactly one folder with that name containing SKILL.md.
# Pinned commits are stored in third-party.lock. Use --update on purpose only.
# Keep total active skills small; measure tokens after each addition.

# --- Process (Matt Pocock; MIT per the repo page) — CORE ---
mattpocock/skills grilling
mattpocock/skills grill-with-docs
mattpocock/skills domain-modeling
mattpocock/skills to-spec
mattpocock/skills to-tickets
mattpocock/skills tdd
mattpocock/skills setup-matt-pocock-skills

# --- Process (optional — enable later if needed) ---
# mattpocock/skills diagnosing-bugs
# mattpocock/skills prototype
# mattpocock/skills handoff
# mattpocock/skills writing-for-agents

# --- Style (OPTIONAL — measure first without them) ---
# Verify each repo's license and read its SKILL.md before enabling.
# caveman: short chat replies only. Does NOT apply to specs, ADRs, tests, map files.
